{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo additional blockers found. The prior submodule-movement and cancellation blockers are fixed. The existing report-provenance defect remains accepted as a low-severity follow-up.\n\nFocused CLI, delivery-reader, race, publication, and engine-identity tests passed, as did `go vet`, build, and artifact-check. Local full-matrix attempts were interrupted; their dispositions below rely on the sealed canonical evidence. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N49\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1623,\n      \"summary\": \"Existing F2: validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in executed Commands and renders their historical outcome and duration without carried_from or carried_generated_at. Consequently, --carry --report presents reused observations in a newly dated report without their origin. This consolidates the unchanged report-provenance findings from earlier rounds.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete spec follow-up F2: exclude carried checks from executed Commands and label reused results with their original head and generation time.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1619-1637 still projects carried commands and historical durations without origin. Recorded here as accepted low-severity follow-up R17-N49; the existing owned F2 is at spec line 254.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1623-1637 retains the reported behavior. This is the same F2 covered by R17-N49, with owner @pose-maintainers and review date 2026-12-15.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N43\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:723-750 witnesses HEAD and every checked-out submodule's HEAD reflog length. validate.go:1046 and 1449-1450 compare the witnesses. TestValidateSubmoduleMovingAndReturningIsNotClean passed in go test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material', including the focused race run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N45\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1463-1468 observes runCtx cancellation independently of check results; lines 1478-1480 fail the run. validate_carry.go:96-97 refuses cancelled bases, and lines 698-703 clear cleanliness and all material bindings. TestCarryRefusesABaseCancelledAtRunLevel and TestCancellationMakesBindingsUnavailable passed in the focused normal and race runs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1619-1637 still omits carried provenance from report summaries. This duplicate of F2 is covered by accepted follow-up R17-N49.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete implementation diff, spec R1-R10 and D1-D3, ADR, CLI help, English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold changes, result serialization, and delivery-reader integration. Swept base eligibility, dirty material, cancellation, pinned HEAD and submodule continuity, gitlinks, rename and quoted names, tracked and ignored symlink aliases, case behavior, dependency confinement, nested and root modules, manifest-free moduleOverrides, stack/check changes and matrix identity, policy widening, duplicate IDs, missing prior results, carried failures, chained provenance, administrative exclusions, and canonical publication under the existing write guard. Examined the existing administrative-material contract and module-metadata knowledge decision. Focused normal and race tests, reader tests, publication/identity tests, vet, build, diff checks and artifact-check passed. Artifact-check reported 985 warnings and resolved its trailer range to 132dcaf7 rather than the sealed subject; its strict exit status was 0. Local full-matrix runs were interrupted and do not constitute independent full-matrix passes. Sealed canonical evidence supplies those results. Persistent discovery, integration and debt assessments were not run because no writable scratch checkout was available. No new blocker was established; F2 remains the accepted report-provenance follow-up. Repository status remained clean.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified the eligibility predicates, selection rules, origin preservation and conservative refusals in code and focused tests. D1 still assumes declared dependencies and selfContained accurately describe check inputs, and the existing material contract excludes ignored products and administrative record data. Those are explicit instance responsibilities, not independently inferred guarantees. Report provenance is accepted separately as R17-N49. Spec F1's complete seal/verify/closeout fixture remains an acknowledged coverage follow-up; this review independently exercised the delivery reader rather than that entire journey.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected silent carried entries, signal observation, failure exit, material invalidation and guarded canonical publication. Focused race tests and publication tests passed. The existing publisher serializes atomic replacement; this change does not add an independent unguarded writer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The JSON fields are additive, old records remain readable, incompatible bases rerun, and CLI filter combinations are explicitly rejected. The delivery reader uses per-check origins.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected malformed metadata, missing or incompatible bases, unsafe revisions, paths, duplicate IDs and unavailable bindings. Focused negative fixtures passed; uncertainty produces a full run with a reason, while invalid CLI combinations return exit 2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced result production into ParseDeliveryValidationRun and the existing publication boundary. Independently ran the carried-head reader test. The broader sealed delivery integration result supplies integration evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R17-N49\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive schema-1 fields, legacy decoding, absent engine identity, CLI help and delivery parsing. Existing records retain their interpretation; eligibility is deliberately stricter for reuse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R17-N49\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97948d92f0ce316e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 preserves an observation's actual head and time while selection establishes unchanged module inputs under the declared ownership contract. D2 rejects whole-matrix or engine changes instead of inventing per-check equivalence. D3 keeps root-change exemptions explicit. The ADR records the structural file-contract and selection trade-off required by R2-R7.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records reuse with retained observation origin, comparable-base eligibility and the explicit selfContained trust boundary.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R17-N49\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R17-N49\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Mapped R1-R10 to parsing/refusal fixtures, eligibility and cleanliness regressions, changed-scope tests, carried-result preservation, counts and engine fields, delivery-reader origin tests and chained carries. Focused tests passed independently. The sealed matrix provides broader build/integration/e2e evidence; the local full matrix was not completed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97948d92f0ce316e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the approved artifacts and non-goals with the implementation diff. Changes remain within validation, shared changed-scope selection, additive result contracts, delivery reading, help and corresponding documentation. No arbitrary command-output cache or per-check input declaration system was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected revision confinement, dependency path checks, alias refusals, administrative-path mode checks, inherited redaction and guarded publication. No new shell interpolation or credential handling was introduced. Focused negative fixtures exercise the cheapest false-pass route: reusing an apparently clean but materially incomparable base. No dedicated carry case was identified in the general adversarial corpus; the carry fixtures provide the specific negative evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97948d92f0ce316e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared reuse of existing module selection and the canonical result with per-check input hashing and manual result merging. The selected design adds conservative eligibility and provenance without a second cache or new input language. The many filesystem refusals reduce availability rather than assert unsupported equivalence. The choice must be revisited if declarations cannot reliably bound inputs, or if those refusals make useful reuse impractical; immutable execution or verified input declarations would then be justified.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently completed with exit 0. Reported 15 claims, 20 observed paths and 985 warnings. Its trailer-resolved head was 132dcaf7a9d5fa82cc438be01f500cfe6698ff8c, not the sealed subject; this was treated as the stated existing attribution behavior, not as proof that the bundle subject changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97948d92f0ce316e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess design --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json. It completed with the sealed design input digest and the ADR governance-contract delta. No repository change resulted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:git status --short\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Discovery persists assessment state. No writable scratch checkout was available, and the task forbids changing the sealed repository.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:git status --short\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists outputs, so it was not invoked in the sealed checkout without writable scratch. Integration was examined through source tracing, independent reader tests and the sealed integration results.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:git status --short\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists outputs and no writable scratch checkout was available. A direct marker scan of the changed carry, scope, result and reader implementation found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion verification must follow POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion; this execution was instructed not to record an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the resulting attestation, which POSE records after consuming this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completed successfully and selected the backend-go, security and documentation-style rules and review workflow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition relies on the sealed canonical strict-matrix producer result, as permitted by the brief. The independent pose validate --strict attempt was interrupted with exit 130 before completion and is not represented as a local pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition relies on the sealed canonical component validation result. The independent pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp attempt was interrupted and returned cancellation failure; it is not a local full-matrix pass. Independent focused normal/race tests, delivery-reader and publication/identity tests, go vet ./... and go build ./... passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
